WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:05.700
Under Windows authentication, the DBA team
owned database access almost by default.

2
00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:10.141
In the target, one connection depends
on a group the identity team built,

3
00:00:10.141 --> 00:00:14.883
a rule the data owner approved, a permission
only a privileged role can grant,

4
00:00:14.883 --> 00:00:19.775
a login the DBAs created, and a connection
string the application team changed.

5
00:00:19.775 --> 00:00:22.699
Miss any owner and the
gap shows up as drift,

6
00:00:22.699 --> 00:00:25.288
or as a help desk call nobody can close.

7
00:00:25.288 --> 00:00:27.600
So the model is one decider per row.

8
00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:30.530
Data leadership decides
verdicts and closure;

9
00:00:30.530 --> 00:00:35.488
the authorizing official decides every
exception; the CISO sets the standard.

10
00:00:35.488 --> 00:00:39.599
The first step is filling the
project's open sponsor and lead roles.

11
00:00:39.599 --> 00:00:41.520
So what does each team actually do?
